{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>To Egypt we gave hand</b> – The dagesh in the nun of נתנו is in place of the root nun, for this nun is a sign of the speakers [1st person plural]. And giving the hand is an oath: וְהִנֵּה נָתַן יָדוֹ (Ezekiel 17:18), and the meaning is like striking palms, for they swore to Egypt and Assyria. Or perhaps we swore:"], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The Hebrew ends with the single word נשׂבע (\"we swore\"), seemingly an incomplete or alternate ending; rendered as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:11.822807566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}